# API Gateway routes

HTTP APIs have a 300-route quota. `ANY` intercepts CORS `OPTIONS` and JWT returns 401, so the browser shows a network error.

## New endpoint under an existing prefix

Do **not** add a Terraform route. Handle it in the Lambda with `rawPath` + HTTP method.

Existing prefixes: `/contact-center/{proxy+}`, `/bots/{botId}/telephony/{proxy+}`, `/telephony/{proxy+}`, `/v1/{proxy+}`, `/email-marketing/{proxy+}`.

```typescript
// GET /contact-center/queues/stats → already covered
if (path === "/queues/stats" && method === "GET") {
  return ok(stats);
}
```

## New top-level prefix

Add one group in `local.http_proxy_groups` (not `explicit_routes`):

```hcl
foo = {
  path         = "/foo/{proxy+}"
  methods      = ["GET", "POST", "PUT", "DELETE"]
  invoke_arn   = var.foo_invoke_arn
  function_arn = var.foo_function_arn
  protected    = true
}
```

Never use `ANY`. Only list methods the Lambda actually serves. Public webhooks that must skip JWT stay as explicit routes (more specific than `{proxy+}`).
